From: jopdop30 <jopdop30@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:44:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] Project scope: sub-projects inherit access from their
 parent

A restricted user who manages or is crew on a project now also reaches
all its sub-projects, to any depth (cycles of parents are guarded).
Being on a sub-project still doesn't reach its parent or siblings.

The sidebar, projects page and api/projects/list.php nest sub-projects
under their parents; for a restricted user, a sub-project whose parent
is out of reach is now listed at top level instead of vanishing. The
crew vacancies page no longer names a parent project out of reach.

Tests: children and grandchildren via manager and via crew, a parent
the user isn't on with a child they are crew on, a sibling, asset
add/remove on sub-projects, unrestricted users unchanged, and a cycle.

Docs: behaviour, audit, checklist, and the decision to leave inventory
values visible to restricted users.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
